  "provenance": "Structure derived by regex over the raw word/document.xml (question headers, instruction lines) plus numbering.xml, independently of any reader under test and before one existed. Kind and option count are proposals from the paper's stated format ('mark the letter A, B, C or D'), not measurements. Answer keys are proposed as absent: the body ends at 'THE END' with no key table, no key string and no marked options. Verified against the source document by the repository owner on 2026-07-26, who confirmed all six load-bearing facts: forty questions numbered 1 to 40; passage groups Q1-10, Q11-16, Q17-21, Q22-27 and Q28-35; Q36-40 each carrying their own sentence set and therefore ungrouped; exactly four options A to D on every question; every question plain multiple choice; and no answer key stated anywhere in the document. The structure and answerKeys layers are verified on that basis. The optionText layer stays unlabelled by design: this document is OCR output with damaged Vietnamese diacritics, so a verbatim reference would encode the damage and exact-match fidelity would score a reader on reproducing corruption. Introduce that layer with the first cleanly authored corpus document instead. Review routing was verified from the confirmed absence of every answer key: each objective question requires teacher confirmation before publish.",
